---
description: Use for component, composable, utility, style, dependency-boundary, or non-trivial refactoring work. Do not use for a localized copy, metadata, or assertion change with no boundary impact.
globs:
  - "app/components/**/*"
  - "app/composables/**/*"
  - "app/utils/**/*"
  - "app/assets/**/*"
  - "server/**/*"
  - "shared/**/*"
  - "test/**/*"
  - "eslint.config.mjs"
  - ".dependency-cruiser.cjs"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Keep UI components focused on rendering and local interaction. Keep reusable
  transformation logic in utilities, browser lifecycle concerns in composables,
  and HTTP delivery at Nitro route boundaries.
- Treat roughly 200–300 lines as a signal to find an ownership seam, not as a
  mechanical split threshold. Document debt and change only the active surface.
- At a feature or package boundary, expose an intentional named public surface
  through an entry point or barrel. Keep feature-private modules direct and do
  not imply that every unmarked export is public.
- Keep imports directional and acyclic: use `pnpm deps:check` for declared
  boundaries and `pnpm deps:cycles` as an independent cycle check.
- Make a file's role clear from its path and name (`entity`, `repository`,
  `adapter`, `facade`, `service`, or feature-private `*.config`), not from a
  reader reverse-engineering its implementation.
- Keep a helper local until two independent callers need a framework-neutral,
  stable input/output contract; then move it to an explicit shared module.
- Put tuning and business constants in a feature-private `*.config` module or
  an intentional repository-level configuration module rather than scattering
  them inline through control flow.
- Make the data path visible in signatures: input → transformation → output.
  Keep side effects at rendering, route, or integration boundaries rather than
  hidden inside transformations.
- Verify cyclomatic complexity with ESLint (limit 8) and cognitive complexity
  with SonarJS (limit 15); introduce the cognitive rule as a warning in an
  existing codebase, then promote it only after reviewing the baseline. Reduce
  a function by ownership and control-flow seams, not cosmetic extraction.
- Reuse the smallest existing abstraction that fits. Introduce a global store,
  manager, provider, dependency, or architectural layer only for a real shared
  boundary with an explicit need.
- Keep 3D scenes isolated under `app/components/scenes/` and preserve their
  semantic, non-canvas fallback and lifecycle controls.
